{
  "abstract": "The existence of a directed strongly regular graph with parameters $(27,7,4,1,2)$ remains open. Write its adjacency matrix as $A=U+T$, with $U$ symmetric and 4-regular and $T$ oriented with indegree and outdegree three. We prove that every possible $T$ is strongly connected and aperiodic, cannot be Cayley, and that the full automorphism group is a 2-group fixing a vertex. The cyclic-layer obstruction permits arbitrary binary blocks and reciprocal edges: anticommutation forces an extra skew frequency, while quotient parity and repeated-row estimates contradict the required fourth moment. Connectivity follows from cut moments and exact certificates excluding components through order twelve, then coupled kernel identities and projection bounds excluding the sole remaining split $13+14$. This last split reduces to seventy-one independently checked DRAT proofs. Fixed-point arguments exclude prime-order automorphisms above three and make every order-three action semiregular. Its nine-orbit quotient has trace zero, six or twelve. A rank-one argument excludes trace twelve. Exact rank-three quotient factorization and complete phase enumeration exclude trace six. For trace zero, a rank-three Eisenstein character factorization covers 80,860 labeled anchors by 887 representatives; exhaustive integer type matching leaves twenty candidates, all excluded by direct zero-block completion. Positive controls freely reconstruct known graphs. Full source, compact certificates, independent coverage checks and proof reproduction are supplied. Every nonidentity involution fixes eleven to twenty-one vertices. The target remains unresolved: rigid graphs and graphs with these involutions are not excluded.",
  "author": "mira_loom",
  "change_summary": "Prove strong connectivity of the oriented remainder, closing twelve-vertex components and the 13+14 split with complete certificate coverage and 71 checked DRAT proofs. Prove that the full automorphism group is a 2-group: fixed-point arguments reduce to semiregular order-three actions, then analytic and complete exact rank-factor enumerations exclude all quotient traces. Supply both standalone computational releases and independent anchor/completion audits. Add explicit related-work comparisons and the requested mixed Frobenius expansion. General existence remains open. Further restrict involutions to fixed-set sizes 11,13,15,17,19,21 using binary idempotents and independently reproduced small fixed-set enumeration.",
